%% Query Processing Flow — From raw input to execution plan
%% Shows how complex/ambiguous queries are decomposed

sequenceDiagram
    actor Student
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant GW as Gateway
    participant NORM as Input Normalizer
    participant ENTITY as Entity Extractor
    participant INTENT as Intent Classifier
    participant DECOMP as Query Decomposer
    participant PLAN as Execution Planner
    participant AGENTS as Agent Dispatcher

    Student->>FE: Complex query (text / voice / doc)
    FE->>GW: POST /api/v1/chat

    Note over NORM: Layer 1: Normalize<br/>(rule-based, <5ms)
    GW->>NORM: Raw input + user_id + session
    Note over NORM: - Text cleanup<br/>- Language detection<br/>- Multi-modal → text conversion

    Note over ENTITY: Layer 2: Extract entities<br/>(LLM structured output, ~200ms)
    NORM->>ENTITY: Normalized text
    Note over ENTITY: Extract structured fields:<br/>- skills: ["Transformer", "LLM"]<br/>- career_goal: "AI Engineer at Google"<br/>- constraints: {timeline: "6 months"}<br/>- experience: "AI-RAN research"<br/>- difficulty_pref: null

    Note over INTENT: Layer 3: Classify intent<br/>(LLM → SLM in V2, ~100ms)
    ENTITY->>INTENT: Entities + original text
    Note over INTENT: Multi-label classification:<br/>- career_guidance: 0.9<br/>- skill_gap_analysis: 0.8<br/>- learning_path: 0.7<br/>- course_search: 0.6<br/>(not mutually exclusive)

    Note over DECOMP: Layer 4: Decompose<br/>(LLM, ~300ms)
    INTENT->>DECOMP: Intents + entities + text
    Note over DECOMP: Break into sub-tasks:<br/>1. Map "AI Engineer at Google" → required skills<br/>2. Gap analysis: user skills vs required<br/>3. Find courses for each gap<br/>4. Build 6-month learning path<br/>5. Synthesize recommendation

    Note over PLAN: Layer 5: Plan execution<br/>(rule-based DAG, <5ms)
    DECOMP->>PLAN: Sub-task list with dependencies
    Note over PLAN: Build DAG:<br/>CAA(1) → SGA(2) → RA(3) → LPPA(4) → LA(5)<br/>Parallel where possible:<br/>CAA + SGA can run concurrently<br/>if no data dependency

    PLAN->>AGENTS: Execution plan (ordered task list)
    Note over AGENTS: Execute per plan,<br/>pass outputs between agents
